WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.325
Unit 1 is the digest as code.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:05.905
The digest script reads a
collection and the routing state,

3
00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.950
and writes a page in five sections.

4
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:13.288
One: open notices by provider, counted
by kind and by action required.

5
00:00:13.288 --> 00:00:17.385
Two: action required, soonest
due first, with the assignment

6
00:00:17.385 --> 00:00:21.650
group the routing named, or the
word digest when there's no task.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.663
Three: maintenance and changes
starting in the next thirty days.

8
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:28.022
Four: what's new in the last seven days,

9
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:30.775
by the first-seen time
in the routing state.

10
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:34.698
And five: what closed or stopped
being listed in the last seven days,

11
00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:38.050
including notices the provider
simply stopped listing.

12
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.890
It writes the page as
Markdown for the owners,

13
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.188
a spreadsheet file with each notice's
route and owner, and a manifest.

14
00:00:45.188 --> 00:00:47.120
The window lengths are parameters,

15
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.050
and in the scheduled run they come
from the settings file's digest block.

16
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.031
The guide's validation
for the digest is simple:

17
00:00:54.031 --> 00:00:57.770
every action-required notice
shows its due date and owner.
